      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To ascertain the hard event rate in local population with normal myocardial perfusion."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The study, which was conducted from August 2006 to January 2007, included 300 patients with normal exercise myocardial perfusion scan (MPS). Patients were categorized according to their pre-test probabilities for CAD. Patients with low pre-test probability for CAD were 136 and ranked in group A, while group B constituted 164 patients who had intermediate to high pre-test probability."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "During a follow-up of mean duration of 27 +/- 3 months, an overall hard cardiac event rate of 1.02% was noted. However, a statistically non-significant difference between the survival rates of low and high pre-test probability groups was also observed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The study demonstrated good prognosis for patients with normal exercise myocardial perfusion scan."
        }
      ]},
